Z||000001||TI_3VOM||06-21-2001||02:16 PM||||Just leave he plate off! IMO, it gives the Fiero a buck-tooth appearance. So unless you're Bugs Bunny, married to your cousin/sister/brother, or (as in my state) required to have plates displayed at both front and rear, the just leave it off.<P>P.S. If you have to have a front plate, feel free to use my handle; it gives that slow poke in front of you an important message in their mirror.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||06-21-2001||02:31 PM||||HA! I just realized what your name means! Very cool!<P>The 87-88 front tag brackets look better. My girlfriend has hre Florida Gator tag on the front of the coupe she has been driving. It looks pretty good except we live in Vol Country!<P>Personally, I hate tags on the front of cars. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||06-21-2001||03:38 PM||||Shhhhhhh.  Don't tell anybody, but I've never had a front plate.  I don't think too many police bother with it unless they use cameras in the area that would need the front plate to I.D. you for running a red light or speeding.  I don't think I'd get away with it up in San Jose CA. like I do down here in Monterey.<BR>  Stupid me.  I ran out of gas on the freeway up in Sacramento last weekend and got away with a warning a scolding from the pretty highway patrolwomen and no mention about not having a front plate.  Only about my pocket knife being too big.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">(she searched me) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||06-21-2001||04:54 PM||||The old 'running out of gas' routine! Just to get searched by a pretty girl in uniform.. At least you had your big knife with you... Reminds me of the scene from Days Of Thunder.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||06-21-2001||07:04 PM||||Yeah, she must of thought I was a major red neck with a couple knives on me and a NRA sticker in my back window.  Good thing she didn't look in my trunk.  It was locked away properly, but my gun was bigger than hers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  She could have written a few tickets if whe wanted too, but she was nice enough to let me go.  I don't think she could have ever guessed I'm a tech. in the computer field.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Besides, WHAT TIMING! my ignition switch broke, so getting gas wouldn't have helped much since I couldn't put power to it.  Had to get it towed.(not impounded) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> $115.00 and a couple days later, I'm back on the road.<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||RobertVol||06-21-2001||11:02 PM||||Did someone say "Vol"?  he he <P>UH How could you let your girl put a [Cough] $$#!!!%!# Gutter(Gator) tag on the Fiero?!?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>lets see.....<BR> how many days till we get our tails kicked in Gainesville?? <P>oh yeah ! thats another board!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Sorry <P>I personally don't like tags on the front of my car but they do look better with the GT nose or 87-88 coupe nose. anything prior looks kinda of strange IMHO... but then again everyone has different tastes.<P><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RobsGT2.jpg"> ||||reg||6
